speechtext:
Mr. Speaker, the answer to the first part of this question is that due dates of payments and amounts are:
(a)	On or before the signing of the agreement for sale, March 14, 1959, $1,101,435.63;
(b)	Ten monthly instalments of $50,000 each commencing April 30, 1959, $500,000;
(c)	Four quarterly instalments of $25,000 each commencing June 15, 1959, $100,000;
(d)	For entitlement of conveyance of four parcels of land, $459,042.55;

(e)	Two half yearly interest payments September 15, 1959 and March 15, 1960, $241,908.46.
In reply to the second part of the question I may say that all payments have been made on due date or within the 30 days' grace allowed by the sale agreement.

